[[File:Macro Builder Button.png|thumb|Macro Builder Button]]
The Macro Builder is a powerful advanced automation tool, which can be used to automate sequences of in-game actions using logic blocks. It is unlocked by reaching {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity|link=Eternity}} for the first time ([[Achievements|{{Keyword|ach|Achievement #070|}}]]). 


__toc__

== Macro Builder Workspace Overview ==
The macro builder can be accessed via the ''Macro'' button located at the bottom-right of the [[Revolution]] screen, next to [[Credits]]. 

On the left side is the macro builder workspace for the currently selected macro slot. Macro blocks can be added, modified, or rearranged to define a desired sequence of actions.

On the right side is a panel with configuration options and information for the currently selected macro slot. 
[[File:Macro Builder Workspace.png|thumb|The Macro Builder Workspace]]
From top to bottom on the right panel:
* Current Macro Slot: When the macro builder is first unlocked, a total of 3 macros slots are available. The dropdown menu will change the currently selected macro slot and the [[File:Add 64.png|20x20px]] button will create a new macro (if a slot is available). Additional macro slots can be purchased for [[Soul Shop|{{keyword|soul|5000}}]] {{icon|soul_icon}} each.
* Macro Name: Displays the currently selected macro slot name. Can be edited using the pencil button.
* Loop Mode: Displays the current loop mode for the macro slot. There are 3 types of loop: Once[[File:Once loop mode.png]], Loop [[File:Loop mode.png]] and Ping Pong[[File:Pingpong loop mode.png]]. "Once" will execute the macro only once, "Loop" will execute the macro in a continuous loop until stopped, and "Ping Pong" will run the macro from top to bottom, and then bottom to top, back and forth.
* Startup Execution: When enabled, the currently selected macro will automatically run when you open the game, after a delay of 30 seconds.
* Logs: Enable to show a window that displays logs when the currently selected macro is run. Useful for debugging macros.
* The Execution Bar: A button to start/stop/pause the current macro. Also displays the macro's current status.

In the bottom-right corner, the current macro can be exported in the form of revoscript, or import revoscript into the macro (both export and import use the device's clipboard). There's also an option to delete the macro, which deletes all blocks in the current macro, but does not remove the macro slot.

== Blockdex ==
[[File:Blockdex.png|thumb|184x184px|The Blockdex]]
When adding a block to the current macro, the Blockdex will appear. The Blockdex is a list of all available blocks which can be added to a macro to perform specific actions.

Currently, there are a total of 30 blocks available, separated into categories: Conditional Blocks, Execution/Loop, Awaiters, In-game Events Blocks and Notifications.

