== In-game scripting ==
To add a block, either click on the "Add a block" button to add a block at the bottom of the macro, or the macro button [[File:Macro Icon.png|24x24px]] on each block to add a new block directly below it.
[[File:A Macro block example.png|thumb|633x633px|An example Macro Block]]
On each macro block, you can:

* Duplicate the block using [[File:Copy 64.png|23x23px]]. The duplicated block will be added directly below the selected block.
* Add a new block directly below it using [[File:Macro Icon.png|24x24px]].
* Move the block up or down using [[File:Arrow Up.png|24x24px]] or [[File:Arrow Down.png|23x23px]].
* Delete the block using [[File:Cross 64.png|21x21px]].
* Additionally, some macro blocks have additional parameters; either dropdown, checkbox, or textbox which can be changed accordingly.
[[File:Macro Break Loop.png|thumb|Special case when an If block is inside a Repeat block - the Break block becomes available]]
Special cases exist for some macro blocks:

* For If, Wait Until and Repeat Until blocks, there's an option to add one or more conditions using [[File:Add 64.png|20x20px]]. Multiple conditions can be combined with the AND, OR, and XOR operators.
* For If, Repeat and Repeat Until blocks, blocks can be added inside the loop or conditions by clicking on the [[File:Macro Icon.png|23x23px]] button at the bottom-left of the block.
* For If block, there's an option to add more logic branches using the "Else If" and "Else" buttons.
* If the Wait Until or If blocks are inside a Repeat block, there's an option to break out of/exit the loop after the conditions of the block are met, by adding a "Break" block.

== Macro Settings ==
[[File:Macro Settings.png|thumb|170x170px|Macro Settings]]
Macro settings can be accessed by clicking the [[File:Option 64.png|23x23px]] button in the bottom-left corner of the panel on the right.

From top to bottom:
* Start with a macro slot: The macro slot will switch to the selected macro on startup (when the game is launched).
* Logs permanent: When enabled, overrides individual macro's settings for displaying logs, such that logs are always displayed.
* Notification from Macro: Enables/disables in-game notification pop-ups from macro actions. For example, disabling this will prevent the pop-ups for challenge completions, when completed by a macro.
* Scroll on Play mode: Enables/disables the automatic scrolling to follow the macro when the macro is running. This is enabled by default, but can be disabled if preferred/to assist with debugging macros.

== Prebuilt Macros ==
Macros can be imported by copying a revoscript macro code into the device's clipboard, then clicking on the import button in the macro builder. 

''For prebuilt macros for different purposes, see [[Macro Templates]].''

